# Elena Vasquez vs Elena Crane

## Current Model

Two **Elenas** serve different scopes at HarborLine and must not be conflated in retrieval. **Elena Vasquez** is Fleet Maintenance Director — on 2026-05-18 she opened the **SG-REFIT drydock** with **drydock window 2026-05-18** starting now, making berth 4 heavy-lift zone Seaglass-only through refit sea trial; Victor Hale confirmed spare thrust bearing staged port-side with **hull penetration** deferred to morning sync. **Elena Crane** is Pier 7 Passenger Services Manager — on 2026-05-27 she escalated a **noise complaint** from **Surfside Condos** about early-morning **pier 7 ramp** grinding before 0700, prompting Juno to schedule quiet-hours enforcement (no impact tools before 0800 weekdays, 0900 weekends) while the commuter **09:30 cutoff** still applies for blocking work.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-18-drydock-window-opens` - Elena Vasquez opens **SG-REFIT drydock** officially; **drydock window 2026-05-18** starts now; berth 4 heavy-lift zone Seaglass-only through refit sea trial; Victor Hale confirms spare **thrust bearing** port-side — no **hull penetration** until sign-off; fuel systems discussion deferred to morning sync.
- `2026-05-27-surfside-noise-escalation` - Elena Crane forwards **noise complaint** from **surfside condos** re **pier 7 ramp** work — grinding before 0700; building rep attached decibel readings threatening city permit review; Juno schedules **quiet hours** enforcement starting tomorrow; commuter **09:30 cutoff** still applies for blocking work.

## Use In Work

- Route "Elena approved drydock" and fleet-impacting SG-REFIT milestones to Elena Vasquez; route Pier 7 passenger noise, ramp messaging, and Surfside Condos complaints to Elena Crane.
- When a query mentions only "Elena," check codename context — drydock/thrust bearing → Vasquez; ramp/noise/commuter rush → Crane.

## Limits

This disambiguation covers the two Elenas only — Victor Hale and Victor Dunn require a separate Victor split. Neither Elena owns Pier 9 infrastructure staging; that routes to Victor Dunn.

