# Juno Castillo ↔ Priya Nandakumar Drill Alignment

## Current Model

Juno Castillo implements Priya Nandakumar's SSB-DRILL rules but owns the working **Storm Surge Weekend Coverage Matrix** that drifted from Priya's official packet. At the May 29 alignment meeting Juno admitted she **manually edited** the working **weekend coverage matrix** to **3 deckhands** per pier, citing volunteer pool realism after May 24 weekend no-shows. Priya's official **source notes** still specified **4 deckhands** — she was not looped on the edit. Marcus Holt noted the sailing grid was built against Juno's 3-headcount version and needed reconciliation before the May 31 drill simulation weekend.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-29-coverage-matrix-drift` - Juno admits she **manually edited** working **weekend coverage matrix** to **3 deckhands** per pier after May 24 weekend no-shows; Priya: official **source notes** still say **4 deckhands** — not looped on edit; Marcus: sailing grid built against Juno's 3-headcount version, needs reconciliation before May 31 drill.

## Use In Work

- Reconcile Juno's working matrix against Priya's source notes before filing the SSB-DRILL after-action review — cite 4 deckhands from official packet unless explicitly referencing Juno's edited working copy.
- Loop Priya on any future coverage matrix edits before updating Marcus Holt's sailing grid for simulation weekends.

## Limits

This drift covers deckhand headcount only — life-vest 45-minute spot checks and Highwater radio codename rules remain Priya's authoritative packet regardless of matrix edits. Juno's edit was not back-propagated to Priya's official SSB-DRILL submission.

